course: dictionary
lesson: 4799
title: Humidity in the air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humidity is how much water vapour is in the air. Water vapour is water that has turned into an invisible gas, so you cannot see it. «A weather station uses temperature, humidity and pressure sensors and code to record readings.» Temperature and pressure are things we measure, and humidity is on that list too, so it is a measured part of the weather.
explain: Use the context clues to check your meaning. The sentence says a station records readings with sensors, so humidity must be something that can be measured. Try your meaning in the sentence: «A weather station uses temperature, humidity and pressure sensors» still makes sense if humidity means the amount of water vapour in the air.
explain: Humidity is also a feeling. On a hot, muggy day the air feels damp and sticky because it holds a lot of water vapour. Sweat dries slowly in that air, so you feel hotter than the thermometer says.
fact: Humidity means the amount of water vapour in the air.
fact: Water vapour is water in the form of an invisible gas.
fact: A hygrometer is the tool used to measure humidity.
fact: «Relative humidity» is given as a percent: how full the air is with water vapour compared with the most it can hold at that temperature.
fact: High humidity makes hot days feel hotter, because sweat dries slowly.
exercise: In «A weather station uses temperature, humidity and pressure sensors and code to record readings.», what is humidity? | The name of the weather station | Water that has turned to ice | *Something measured to record the weather | A cold metal bar used to hold the sensors
exercise: What is water vapour? | Water that has frozen into snow | Salty water from the sea | Rain falling from the clouds | *Water in the form of an invisible gas in the air
exercise: What does a hygrometer measure? | Wind speed | Rainfall in millimetres | Temperature in a room | *Humidity, the water vapour in the air
test: Why does high humidity make a hot day feel hotter? | Because the sun is closer to the ground | *Because sweat dries slowly in damp air | Because the air is colder | Because the wind has stopped
test: What does «relative humidity» of 80% mean? | The air is 80% water | There is an 80% chance of rain | *The air holds 80% of the most water vapour it could hold at that temperature | The temperature is 80 degrees
exam: Which sentence uses humidity correctly? | *The humidity of the air was 80%, so the day felt sticky | I put on humidity before I went out | The humidity of the classroom is 12 metres long | Her humidity was a sad song
